 Studies"},{"text":"Development policy"}],[{"text":"MA International Relations"},{"text":"Foreign policy"}],[{"text":"Master of Public Administration"},{"text":"Government/public administration"}],[{"text":"MSc Data Science"},{"text":"Policy analytics"}],[{"text":"MA Sociology"},{"text":"Social policy"}],[{"text":"MA International Development"},{"text":"Development research"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Political Economy/Public Policy","MA/MSc Public Policy/Economics","Think Tank Research","Policy Analyst","Senior Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"Students targeting highly quantitative policy research should prioritise econometrics, statistics, causal inference, R/Python and research design."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"France"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Singapore"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant Master's Programmes"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Master of Public Policy"},{"text":"Master of Public Administration"},{"text":"MSc Political Economy"},{"text":"MSc Economics"},{"text":"International Development"},{"text":"Development Economics"},{"text":"International Affairs"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Public Administration"},{"text":"Public Economics"},{"text":"Data & Public Policy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For competitive international policy careers, strong quantitative preparation, research experience, writing samples and relevant internships can be as important as the degree itself."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A typical research pathway:"},{"type":"h","text":"BA Political Economy / Public Policy / Governance"},{"type":"h","text":"Research/Policy Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Poli